Description: Implements one-sample t-tests for a Gaussian mean with unknown
    variance using Ville and extended Ville calibration. Supports Gaussian,
    Cauchy, Student-t5, Laplace and horseshoe effect-size priors, one-sided
    and two-sided alternatives, and separately calibrated Lebesgue benchmarks.
    Provides Monte Carlo calibration matching the accompanying Python
    simulations, deterministic calibration, running values, first rejection
    times, summaries and plots. Finite Monte Carlo calibration approximates
    the population calibration and reports sampling and numerical diagnostics.
